Was a great night last night getting to make that walk to the cage once again. Not my best performance to date but a win none the less. Thankful to God for the victory and thankful to everyone for their support at the arena or on the PPV. I know I have to keep climbing and improving. I am happy but not content, there is no time for celebration or rest. I know my potential and skill and will keep working until I can fully tap into it. Whatever that takes.  Kobe Bryant once said “Those times when you get up early and you work hard; those times when you stay up late and you work hard; those times when you don’t feel like working, you’re too tired, you don’t want to push yourself, but you do it anyway; that is actually the dream. That’s the dream. It’s not the destination, it’s the journey.” 
Huge shout out to my team for being in my corner and pushing me everyday. Pinpointing my flaws and giving great guidance and instruction. The sky is truly the limit and I’m blessed to be in the position I am In. Onward and upward. 
