I know most folks are probably sick of seeing their feeds full of Aurora photos, BUT, I can hardly believe it, I witnessed my very first Aurora in the wee hours of this morning.

I missed both over the last few days due to weather and me not wanting to get out in the cold haha

I stepped out at about 1030 3rd June and walked back in the door this morning at 1:30am

Like any good photographer, can't help myself but to download what was captured. Photos will be another day though.

This is 2 short clips from East Coast Tasmania, bared the wind and chill, thermos in hand.

I was only going to get photos, which I got plenty of, but then I decided to snap a few timelapse, spanning over 1.5 hours.

How absolutely beautiful this was to witness.

Taken on the Nikon Z9 with 14-24mm
