Tasmanian Summers ❤️

Question is, when do I come back to roost? 

Home is definitely where the heart is and I have taken a load off the past few weeks and have enjoyed the peacefulness and de-stressed from the crazy traffic of the GC which I detest.

Dad and I grabbed the cameras and took off early to catch what ever was on offer on our way to Abel's Bay. Though this particular morning the gusty wind was kicking up the sand and exfoliating the shins, it was worth watching the surfers catch wave after wave just offshore. The light was licking the back of the waves and illuminating the beautiful reflections, this surfer had some headphones in....I wonder what tunes he was listening to?

