Coaching Team USA at the International Surf Rescue Challenge was one of those experiences that felt surreal. Being welcomed by the team and staff reinforced that I was exactly right where I needed to be. 
Getting to meet some of the coaches and athletes for the first time was a highlight.  Just as meaningful was continuing to build strong rapport with our own athletes, along with competitors and coaches from other teams. Those shared exchanges, standards, connections on and off the sand is what I enjoyed most. 

Huge thank you to the athletes, team captains, and coaching staff who set the tone from day one. The culture of respect, accountability, and support you created made connection easy and coaching meaningful. Being welcomed into that environment is something I don't take lightly. 

